READ-ONLY verification round. No package source touched, no version bump.
Artifacts: docs/srmech/notes/_v1{,b}_opgaps_verify_rc427.{py,ndjson} (14 records,
rc425, registry 649, numpy absent). G1's own script re-run and its NDJSON
reproduced bit-exact modulo generated_at.

REFUTED
  FA3 decision (ii). The "downstream 13824 vs 5184" is IDENTICAL under BOTH
    conventions — measured on both tables. It is the forward-vs-reversed
    INTERVAL composition inside one table, a different axis from
    dihedral_group's `convention` parameter. G1's own instrument_correction
    records that the convention read could not fire (13824 twice) and then
    substituted this measurement; the spec reports the substitute as evidence
    the two conventions are "distinguishable at both levels". It is not.
  FA3 headline "360 of 576 cells differ" is not independent evidence. The
    h_then_g table IS the transpose of g_then_h, so 360 == 576 − 216 identically
    (216 = the commuting-pair count). It restates non-abelianness; by the
    standing rule a nonzero census is GAUGE.
  The two conventions are ISOMORPHIC: x → x⁻¹ is an isomorphism L → R; class
    count 9/9, class sizes and element-order multisets identical. The decision
    is a LABELLING decision (real for a caller reading T3I·T5I = T10 vs T2),
    not a structural one.
  FC3's "three Moufang identities fail on pairwise-disjoint halves" is
    SPELLING-DEPENDENT. G1's three spellings reproduce exactly (5376 each,
    intersections 2688); an independently chosen equivalent triple gives a
    COINCIDENT pair (5376/5376, symmetric difference 0). "Counts are not sets"
    survives on the M1/M2 pair; the three-way framing does not generalise.
  FC3's "a count-only or boolean read erases that completely" is false for the
    Moufang third — the SHIPPED moufang_residue already returns a per-ordered-
    triple exact-ℚ defect (1176 of 4096 failing at dim 16).

CONFIRMED (independent instruments, not G1's helpers)
  FA1 — no group of order 12 or 24 reachable; orders are powers of two only;
    group_algebra_table refuses dim 3/5/12/24.
  FA2 — 0 word-part transposition/inversion hits in music/relations __all__.
  FA4 — 1507/1507 on forte AND rahn, with a LIVE negative control (rotations-
    only orbit agrees on 919/1507, so the instrument can return otherwise).
  FB1/FB2 — Z/7 49, Z/12 144, Q8 40, D12 216 exact; M16 predicts 144 measures
    88 (error 56); M32 predicts 544 measures 184 (error 360).
  FC5/NC1 — flip_pair(8,1,2) differs from algebra_table(8) in exactly 2 cells;
    flexible 256/256 on the signed loop, 508/512 on the algebra basis.
  FC1c pooled — reconfirmed on an independent 8-law vector.
  Proposal 4's signature asymmetry is live at rc425.

CORRECTIONS TO THE SPEC
  Proposal 4 is INCOMPLETE: loop_invariants(dim=8) also lacks table= and is
    unit_loop's direct downstream consumer.
  conjugacy_census's prior_art_grep omits its nearest shipped neighbour,
    loop_invariants, which already returns center / commutant / nucleus.
  Class assignments: proposal 4's "Class A — addressed by its table" is forced
    (Class A is content-addressing / SHA-256); dihedral_group's prose swaps the
    K/C roles relative to the shipped discipline (the flip is K, the
    re-application is C) even though the code gets it right.

